# ============================================================================
# Multi-cohort single-cell RNA-seq batch pipeline  (v8 — GSE185344 removed)
# ============================================================================
# Each folder = one independent dataset (cohort). For every cohort the script:
#   1. Scans the folder and auto-detects samples + their file format
#   2. Triages duplicate matrices for the same GSM (raw vs processed)
#   3. Loads each sample with the format-appropriate reader
#   4. Merges & preprocesses (Normalize, HVGs, Scale, PCA, neighbours, cluster, UMAP)
#   5. Calls cluster markers (stratified by placeholder genotype = Unknown)
#   6. Annotates cell types via SingleR using a species-matched reference
#   7. Names clusters and draws UMAPs
#   8. Writes every output into THAT cohort's own folder
#   9. Moves on to the next cohort
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHANGES IN v8 — GSE185344 withdrawn from the study
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Removed:
#   * The Adeno_GSE185344 cohort entry.
#   * All serialised-R-object machinery, which existed ONLY to read that
#     series' GSE185344_PH_scRNA.final.rds(.gz):
#       - read_rds_seurat()            reader
#       - load_r_object()              multi-strategy loader
#       - probe_file_magic()           byte-level format probe
#       - classify_magic() / read_magic() / raw_to_text() helpers
#       - check_gzip_intact()          gzip integrity test
#       - triage_duplicate_robjects()  .rds vs .rds.gz selection
#       - rds_stem()                   filename stem helper
#       - the "rds_seurat" sample type and its scan/dispatch branches
#       - cfg$rds_preference, cfg$allow_temp_decompress,
#         cfg$max_decompress_layers, cfg$keep_author_annotations
#       - author annotation transfer, umap_author_annotation.pdf and
#         author_annotations.csv (only RDS objects carried author metadata)
#       - robject_file_comparison.csv output
#   * The ANNOTATION_ONLY_PATTERNS entries that existed for the two GSE185344
#     companion CSVs are retained, since the same guard usefully protects
#     other cohorts from ingesting metadata/TCR tables as expression.
#
# Cohort count is now 18 (8 NEPC + 10 Adenocarcinoma).
#
# NOTE: scan_cohort() still SKIPS any *.rds / *.rda / *.RData it encounters,
# so a stray Seurat object in a folder is ignored rather than misparsed by a
# text reader. Nothing attempts to load it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHANGES CARRIED OVER
#   v3 — raw/processed matrix triage (GSE141445 GSM4203181)
#   v2 FIX 1 — chunked dense->sparse conversion (16 GB limit, GSE181294)
#   v2 FIX 2 — annotation-column sniffing for labelled CSVs
#   v2 FIX 3 — header/data column-offset detection for DGE files
#   Plus: per-sample error capture, gc() between samples, output-file skipping.
#
# Sample formats handled (auto-dispatched):
#   triplet_10x      <pfx>_barcodes.tsv.gz + _features.tsv.gz + _matrix.mtx.gz
#   triplet_custom   <pfx>.barcode.csv.gz  + .genes.csv.gz    + .counts.mtx.gz
#   dense_csv        <pfx>_dense.csv.gz            cells x genes, has CLUSTER col
#   gene_cell_table  <pfx>_gene_cell_exprs_table.txt.gz   Gene_ID + Symbol + cells
#   matrix_txt       <pfx>_dge.txt.gz / data.matrix.txt.gz / data.raw.matrix.txt.gz
#   matrix_csv       <pfx>.count.csv.gz                    genes x cells CSV
#   labelled_csv     matrix + embedded annotation columns
#   archive_tar      <pfx>.tar.gz    wraps a 10x matrix directory
#   archive_zip      <pfx>.zip       wraps a 10x matrix directory
# ============================================================================

